ladies and gentlemen i'm delighted  to be with you at this new economy forum  and i would like to thank you for the  invitation and  i would like to thank in particular mike  bloomberg  for his tireless efforts and generous  contribution  to the global response to this pandemic  as so often he has understood that  we are all in this together  my first message for you today is  that we will only end this pandemic if  we  fight it everywhere in the world  this crisis has shown us that global  public health  is the foundation of the world's  prosperity and security  and it is a prerequisite for recovery  and this is why the european union has  been leading  the global coronavirus response  since the beginning of the pandemic  we've joined forces  with global institutions with partner  countries  charitable foundations but also with  business  and civil society we brought together  more than 40 countries to raise 16  billion euros  and this to finance the development of  vaccines  tests and treatments for the whole world  developing a vaccine against covet 19  is one of the most pressing challenges  of our time  but just finding a vaccine is not enough  we must ensure that  everyone has access to it to end this  pandemic  and this is what the vaccine's pillar  in our global response the so-called  covex facility  aims to achieve safe vaccines  must be available for all whoever they  are  wherever they are whatever they can  afford  no middle or low-income country should  be left behind  and to the few countries hesitating to  join our efforts  i say this is as much a self-interest  investment  as it is a show of solidarity because  a global recovery is the only way  to reopen our economies to restart the  labor market  to repair supply chains and start  rebuilding  my second message is that we must  rebuild  our world better and what we do next  really matters over the next two years  governments around the world will spend  around 10  trillion euros for the recovery  the last time we had a recession  the world invested in piecing back  together  a broken system inequalities  and harmful emissions went up as did  commodity prices  and investments in fossil fuels we  cannot afford to make that same mistake  and as mike bloomberg has rightly said  this is about capitalizing on existing  market forces  not fighting them we need to use our  recovery stimulus to invest in the clean  and digital technologies of the future  to make our economies more resilient and  our societies and job markets  fairer and this  is the thinking behind europe's 1.8  trillion euro recovery package  our recovery plan we call it next  generation  eu will invest 37  in projects linked to our european green  deal  from clean hydrogen to housing  renovations you name it  and it will invest another 20 percent on  digital  from data to infrastructure and new  technologies  and this is how we can recover from this  crisis  and build a healthier and stronger world  for the next generation we can do it  if we do it together you can count on  europe to lead the way  thank you
 

